Interop test data (interop/, not part of the module's packages)
---------------------------------------------------------------

The nested test-only module interop/ fetches, at test time, payloads
recorded from real devices that two projects publish as test fixtures;
none of them is included in this repository:

- aioshelly (github.com/home-assistant-libs/aioshelly, Apache-2.0,
  Copyright the aioshelly contributors), tag 13.34.1: fixtures/ and
  tests/rpc_device/fixtures/shellyplus2pm/.
- Home Assistant core (github.com/home-assistant/core, Apache-2.0,
  Copyright the Home Assistant contributors), commit e8c451ce3967:
  tests/components/shelly/fixtures/.

interop/bthome_test.go installs bthome-ble 3.24.0 (MIT) from PyPI in a
container at test time and runs our script interop/testdata/bthome_peer.py
on it; nothing of bthome-ble is kept here.

Test data
---------

Every device id, MAC address, password, Wi-Fi network, address and URL in
the tests and the examples is a made-up demo value. Model and type codes
are real model names, chosen to exercise each code path. TestShellyDigest
uses the SHA-256 worked example of RFC 7616 section 3.9.1.
